> What if one player goes to another level while the other doesn't?

ditto. I'm aware that having *all* levels active at once might slow
the game down, but I don't see you having more than one level active
at once can do more than increase the number of monstas to be moving
at one time (depending on how many were on each level) in proportion
to the number of levels active...


As far as I can see, your complaints are about implementing a
multihack based on nethack, and I'd agree with you COMPLETELY.  Don't
risk insanity trying it.  Rewrite it, and rewrite it with EVERYTHING
so far in mind, plus some set of wishes that we could compile from
everyone who's interested.

